        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Career guidance theories are simple maps of how people choose work: matching traits to jobs, developing through life stages, learning from experience and using chance events, and each map is useful for a different kind of decision when you test it against real evidence."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Use the matching idea to shortlist, the stages idea to plan timing, the learning idea to test through experience and the chance idea to stay open to opportunities."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Check any claim about careers with live notices and working people."
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "proof",
      "title": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test"
